

Choose option A: ServiceLoader.

Use the official TestNG ServiceLoader mechanism.

Requirements:

1. Keep the core module independent of TestNG.

2. Implement a no-argument constructor that
   initializes the required lifecycle components.

3. Do not introduce a JVM-wide static singleton.

4. Ensure callbacks for all <test> elements
   within one TestNG execution use the same
   adapter instance and shared lifecycle state.

5. Preserve isolation between separate TestNG
   executions in the same JVM.

6. Prevent duplicate registration when tests
   also register the adapter programmatically.

7. Do not migrate existing legacy listeners.

8. Do not modify existing configuration behavior.

Before enabling automatic registration globally,
create an isolated integration test with:

- One suite containing two <test> elements.
- Parallel test execution.
- Separate configuration contexts.
- Verification of adapter identity.
- Verification of final context cleanup.

First report whether the tests demonstrate
the required instance-sharing behavior.

Do not enable global registration until these
checks pass.
